247
00:16:12,940 --> 00:16:13,920
We know that right,

248
00:16:14,540 --> 00:16:15,260
I'm glad.

249
00:16:15,260 --> 00:16:18,100
So one last true-false question:

250
00:16:18,680 --> 00:16:23,200
A board of review represents an opportunity for the troops' committee to learn how well

251
00:16:23,200 --> 00:16:26,460
the troops' adult leaders are delivering the scout program to its youth.

252
00:16:27,140 --> 00:16:28,100
Absolutely true,

253
00:16:28,240 --> 00:16:30,580
And that is what boards of review are all about.

254
00:16:30,720 --> 00:16:33,360
They're certainly not retests of requirements for any reason.

255
00:16:33,920 --> 00:16:35,200
They're definitely conversations,

256
00:16:35,840 --> 00:16:40,380
And many of these conversations just need to focus on the kind of experience the scout is

257
00:16:40,380 --> 00:16:43,980
having and how well the troop is delivering the scouting program as written.

258
00:16:43,980 --> 00:16:47,920
This is a big subject in a lot of ways.

259
00:16:48,160 --> 00:16:54,280
There are lots of sets of questions that people have written for boards of review out there,

260
00:16:54,780 --> 00:16:56,420
Lots of thinking about it,

261
00:16:56,540 --> 00:17:02,940
But the most important thing is what I've just said, that the board of review is a focus

262
00:17:02,940 --> 00:17:08,040
on the kind of experience a scout is having and how well the troop is delivering that program.

263
